        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Naga Chili, Bhut jolokia, ghost pepper, ghost chili, U-morok, red naga, naga jolokia, ghost jolokia, Naga morich\n- Places: Arunachal Pradesh, Assam, Nagaland, Manipur, Bangladesh\n- Concepts: interspecific hybrid chili pepper\n\nFacts:\n- The Naga Chili is closely related to the Bhut jolokia.\n- The Bhut jolokia is also known as ghost pepper, ghost chili, U-morok, red naga, naga jolokia, and ghost jolokia.\n- The Naga Chili is an interspecific hybrid chili pepper.\n- The Naga Chili is cultivated in the Indian states of Arunachal Pradesh, Assam, Nagaland, and Manipur.\n- The Naga Chili is closely related to the Naga morich of Bangladesh.",
